        <activityName xml:lang="en">Bus stop, asphalt pavement, unbound foundation layer, recycling aggregate</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Bus stop, asphalt pavement, unbound foundation layer, recycling aggregate
Modern Swiss and European technologies are applied to regional storage facilities, material extraction, and production processes. 
UUID: 168e2228-49ce-4c0c-b624-7f7a822a9929
This dataset documents the production, installation, deconstruction and end-of-life treatment of 1 m2 unbound foundation layer for bus stop (asphalt pavement) in Switzerland.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Layer thickness 500 mm, service life 40 years.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_168e2228-49ce-4c0c-b624-7f7a822a9929.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
